PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L03U6.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":3,"cefr":"A2a","unit":6,"theme":"Let's Cook!","essential_question":"How does cooking bring families together?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1","title":"Grandma's Date Cookies: Countable, Uncountable, some and any","objectives":["Students will be able to tell countable nouns from uncountable nouns.","Students will be able to use some in positive sentences and any in negatives and questions.","I can say \"some flour\" and \"two eggs\".","I can ask \"Are there any onions?\" and say \"There isn't any milk\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التمييز بين الأسماء المعدودة وغير المعدودة.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام some في الإثبات وany في النفي والسؤال.","أستطيع أن أقول some flour وtwo eggs.","أستطيع أن أسأل Are there any onions? وأقول There isn't any milk."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"recipe","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɛsəpi/","definition":"instructions that tell you how to cook something","arabic":"وصفة طعام","example":"Grandma's recipe for date cookies is a secret.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-W01"},{"word":"ingredient","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈɡridiənt/","definition":"one of the foods you use to make a dish","arabic":"مكوّن","example":"Flour is the main ingredient in bread.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-W02"},{"word":"flour","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈflaʊɚ/","definition":"white or brown powder from wheat, used to make bread and cakes","arabic":"دقيق / طحين","example":"We need two cups of flour.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-W03"},{"word":"sugar","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʃʊɡɚ/","definition":"a sweet white or brown food you add to drinks and cakes","arabic":"سكر","example":"Don't put too much sugar in your tea.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Countable nouns are things we can count: one egg, two eggs; an onion, three onions. They have a singular and a plural.\nUncountable nouns are things we can't count one by one: flour, sugar, butter, milk, water, rice, bread. They have no plural and no a/an: some flour (NOT a flour / flours).\nUse some in positive sentences: There's some sugar. Use any in negatives and questions: There isn't any milk. Are there any eggs? Use some in offers and requests: Would you like some tea? Can I have some water?\ncountable: an egg, two eggs, some eggs, any eggs\nuncountable: some flour, any milk (no a/an, no -s)\nsome → positive sentences, offers, requests\nany → negatives and questions","examples":["There's some rice in the pot.","We need some onions for the soup.","Is there any oil in the bottle?","There aren't any plates on the table.","Would you like some honey?","I don't have any money with me.","Can I have some water, please?","There's some garlic in the fridge."],"common_errors":["✗ I want a bread. → ✓ I want some bread. / I want a loaf of bread. (bread is uncountable.)","✗ We need two rices. → ✓ We need some rice. (rice is uncountable – no plural.)","✗ There isn't some milk. → ✓ There isn't any milk. (Negatives → any.)","✗ Are there some eggs? → ✓ Are there any eggs? (Questions → any (except offers).)"],"arabic":"الأسماء المعدودة نعدّها: an egg / two eggs، وغير المعدودة لا تُعد: flour وsugar وmilk وrice وbread.\nالأسماء غير المعدودة لا نضع معها a ولا نجمعها: some rice وليس rices.\nنستخدم some في الإثبات والعروض والطلبات، وany في النفي والسؤال.\nانتبه: bread غير معدود في الإنجليزية، فنقول some bread أو a loaf of bread."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Grandma's Date Cookies: Countable, Uncountable, some and any”. Let’s learn countable and uncountable nouns; some and any together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U6-LS1 | Grandma's Date Cookies: Countable, Uncountable, some and any","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Grandma's Date Cookies”: Today Sara is helping Grandma Fatimah in the kitchen. They're going to make ma'amoul – date cookies. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Today Sara is helping Grandma Fatimah in the kitchen. They're going to make ma'amoul – date cookies.","visual":"Image GV-L03-U6-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Countable nouns are things we can count: one egg, two eggs; an onion, three onions. They have a singular and a plural. Uncountable nouns are things we can't count one by one: flour, sugar, butter, milk, water, rice, bread. They have no plural and no a/an: some flour (NOT a flour / flours).","on_screen":"countable: an egg, two eggs, some eggs, any eggs • uncountable: some flour, any milk (no a/an, no -s) • some → positive sentences, offers, requests","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. There's some rice in the pot. We need some onions for the soup. Is there any oil in the bottle?","on_screen":"There's some rice in the pot. / We need some onions for the soup. / Is there any oil in the bottle?","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I want a bread.” That’s not right. We say: “I want some bread. / I want a loaf of bread.” bread is uncountable.","on_screen":"✗ I want a bread.   ✓ I want some bread. / I want a loaf of bread.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Can we say \"three flours\"? … Think! … No – flour is uncountable. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"some flour\" and \"two eggs\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"some flour\" and \"two eggs\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: countable and uncountable nouns; some and any.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الأسماء المعدودة نعدّها: an egg / two eggs، وغير المعدودة لا تُعد: flour وsugar وmilk وrice وbread.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I want a bread. — الصحيح: I want some bread. / I want a loaf of bread.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول some flour وtwo eggs."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Grandma's Date Cookies","body":"Today Sara is helping Grandma Fatimah in the kitchen. They're going to make ma'amoul – date cookies.\n\"Do we have any flour?\" Sara asks.\n\"Yes, there's some flour in the cupboard,\" says Grandma. \"We also need some butter, a little sugar and some dates.\"\n\"Are there any eggs?\"\n\"No, there aren't any eggs, but we don't need eggs for this recipe.\"\nSara mixes the flour and butter in a big bowl. Grandma puts some date paste inside each cookie.\nSoon the whole house smells wonderful!","word_count":85,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"There's ___ flour in the cupboard.","options":["some","many","a","any"],"answer":"some","explanation":"some in positive sentences, offers and requests.","explanation_ar":"some للإثبات والعرض والطلب."},{"q":"There aren't ___ eggs in the fridge.","options":["any","some","an","a"],"answer":"any","explanation":"any in negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"any للنفي والسؤال."},{"q":"Is there ___ sugar for the tea?","options":["a","some","an","any"],"answer":"any","explanation":"any in negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"any للنفي والسؤال."},{"q":"Would you like ___ juice?","options":["a","some","any","many"],"answer":"some","explanation":"some in positive sentences, offers and requests.","explanation_ar":"some للإثبات والعرض والطلب."},{"q":"We need ___ onion for the salad.","options":["a","any","some","an"],"answer":"an","explanation":"Countable: a/an + singular, or a plural.","explanation_ar":"المعدود: مفرد مع a أو جمع."},{"q":"","options":["I'd like any bread, please.","I'd like a bread, please.","I'd like some bread, please.","I'd like some breads, please."],"answer":"I'd like some bread, please.","explanation":"Uncountable: no a/an, no plural.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود: بدون a وبدون جمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Countable (C) or uncountable (U)? Write C or U. Word bank: some, any, U, C","items":[{"q":"tomato → ______","options":[],"answer":"C","explanation":"Countable: a/an + singular, or a plural.","explanation_ar":"المعدود: مفرد مع a أو جمع."},{"q":"butter → ______","options":[],"answer":"U","explanation":"Uncountable: no a/an, no plural.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود: بدون a وبدون جمع."},{"q":"spoon → ______","options":[],"answer":"C","explanation":"Countable: a/an + singular, or a plural.","explanation_ar":"المعدود: مفرد مع a أو جمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write some or any. Word bank: some, any, U, C","items":[{"q":"There isn't ______ salt in the soup.","options":[],"answer":"any","explanation":"any in negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"any للنفي والسؤال."},{"q":"Can I have ______ rice, please?","options":[],"answer":"some","explanation":"some in positive sentences, offers and requests.","explanation_ar":"some للإثبات والعرض والطلب."},{"q":"Are there ______ apples in the bag?","options":[],"answer":"any","explanation":"any in negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"any للنفي والسؤال."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Look in your kitchen at home (or imagine). Write sentences.","items":[{"q":"There's some ___ in my fridge.","options":[],"answer":"There's some cheese in my fridge.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable and uncountable nouns; some and any correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"There are some ___ in our kitchen.","options":[],"answer":"There are some bananas in our kitchen.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable and uncountable nouns; some and any correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"There isn't any ___ today.","options":[],"answer":"There isn't any yogurt today.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable and uncountable nouns; some and any correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Are there any ___? (ask a question)","options":[],"answer":"Are there any dates?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable and uncountable nouns; some and any correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Would you like some ___? (an offer)","options":[],"answer":"Would you like some tea?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable and uncountable nouns; some and any correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Shopping list.","items":[{"q":"Write a shopping list for a family breakfast: 3 countable and 3 uncountable things.","options":[],"answer":"eggs, tomatoes, olives; bread, cheese, honey","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable and uncountable nouns; some and any correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about your list with some and any.","options":[],"answer":"We need some eggs. There isn't any cheese. Are there any olives?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable and uncountable nouns; some and any correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Role-play a guest and host. Write 2 offers and answers.","options":[],"answer":"Would you like some coffee? – Yes, please. Would you like some dates? – No, thank you.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable and uncountable nouns; some and any correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Hot Seat","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team sits in the hot seat facing the class.","The teacher shows a cue card behind the student; the team gives a clue using countable and uncountable nouns; some and any without saying the word.","The student in the hot seat guesses the cue word within 30 seconds.","Teams score 1 point for a correct guess and 1 point for a correct clue sentence. Rotate seats."],"data":[{"label":"some flour"},{"label":"any eggs"},{"label":"some apples"},{"label":"any sugar"},{"label":"a lot of rice"},{"label":"many tomatoes"},{"label":"much milk"},{"label":"a few onions"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"There's ___ butter on the table.","options":["many","some","a","any"],"answer":"some","explanation":"some in positive sentences, offers and requests.","explanation_ar":"some للإثبات والعرض والطلب."},{"q":"Are there ___ tomatoes for the salad?","options":["much","some","any","a"],"answer":"any","explanation":"any in negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"any للنفي والسؤال."},{"q":"","options":["We need some sugars.","We need a sugar.","We need any sugar.","We need some sugar."],"answer":"We need some sugar.","explanation":"Uncountable: no a/an, no plural.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود: بدون a وبدون جمع."},{"q":"I don't have ___ homework today!","options":["some","any","many","a"],"answer":"any","explanation":"any in negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"any للنفي والسؤال."},{"q":"Can I have ___ honey, please?","options":["an","a","some","any"],"answer":"some","explanation":"some in positive sentences, offers and requests.","explanation_ar":"some للإثبات والعرض والطلب."},{"q":"","options":["There isn't any spoons in the drawer.","There aren't any spoon in the drawer.","There aren't some spoons in the drawer.","There aren't any spoons in the drawer."],"answer":"There aren't any spoons in the drawer.","explanation":"any in negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"any للنفي والسؤال."},{"q":"Which noun is uncountable?","options":["milk","bowl","egg","onion"],"answer":"milk","explanation":"Uncountable: no a/an, no plural.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود: بدون a وبدون جمع."},{"q":"Which noun is countable?","options":["salt","water","apple","flour"],"answer":"apple","explanation":"Countable: a/an + singular, or a plural.","explanation_ar":"المعدود: مفرد مع a أو جمع."},{"q":"","options":["Would you like a cookies?","Would you like some cookies?","Would you like some cookie?","Would you like any cookies?"],"answer":"Would you like some cookies?","explanation":"some in positive sentences, offers and requests.","explanation_ar":"some للإثبات والعرض والطلب."},{"q":"There ___ any rice left.","options":["isn't","hasn't","don't","aren't"],"answer":"isn't","explanation":"any in negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"any للنفي والسؤال."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Sara and Grandma Fatimah in a warm kitchen making date cookies: a big bowl of dough, a jar of date paste, a bag of flour and a plate of finished cookies. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Sara and Grandma Fatimah in a warm kitchen making date cookies: a big bowl of dough, a jar of date paste, a bag of flour and a plate of finished cookies"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about countable and uncountable nouns; some and any, with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about countable and uncountable nouns"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows recipe (instructions that tell you how to cook something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing recipe: instructions that tell you how to cook something"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows ingredient (one of the foods you use to make a dish); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing ingredient: one of the foods you use to make a dish"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows flour (white or brown powder from wheat, used to make bread and cakes); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing flour: white or brown powder from wheat, used to make bread and cakes"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows sugar (a sweet white or brown food you add to drinks and cakes); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing sugar: a sweet white or brown food you add to drinks and cakes"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Hot Seat”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Hot Seat"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-W01","script":"recipe. recipe. Grandma's recipe for date cookies is a secret.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-W02","script":"ingredient. ingredient. Flour is the main ingredient in bread.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-W03","script":"flour. flour. We need two cups of flour.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-W04","script":"sugar. sugar. Don't put too much sugar in your tea.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-T1","script":"Today Sara is helping Grandma Fatimah in the kitchen. They're going to make ma'amoul – date cookies. \"Do we have any flour?\" Sara asks. \"Yes, there's some flour in the cupboard,\" says Grandma. \"We also need some butter, a little sugar and some dates.\" \"Are there any eggs?\" \"No, there aren't any eggs, but we don't need eggs for this recipe.\" Sara mixes the flour and butter in a big bowl. Grandma puts some date paste inside each cookie. Soon the whole house smells wonderful!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Grandma's Date Cookies: Countable, Uncountable, some and any”. Let’s learn countable and uncountable nouns; some and any together. Listen to the start of “Grandma's Date Cookies”: Today Sara is helping Grandma Fatimah in the kitchen. They're going to make ma'amoul – date cookies. Look at the green words. Countable nouns are things we can count: one egg, two eggs; an onion, three onions. They have a singular and a plural. Uncountable nouns are things we can't count one by one: flour, sugar, butter, milk, water, rice, bread. They have no plural and no a/an: some flour (NOT a flour / flours). Here are some examples. There's some rice in the pot. We need some onions for the soup. Is there any oil in the bottle? Be careful! Some learners say: “I want a bread.” That’s not right. We say: “I want some bread. / I want a loaf of bread.” bread is uncountable. Quick check: Can we say \"three flours\"? … Think! … No – flour is uncountable. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"some flour\" and \"two eggs\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2","title":"How Much Sugar? How Many Eggs? much, many, a lot of","objectives":["Students will be able to use many with countable nouns and much with uncountable nouns in questions and negatives.","Students will be able to ask How much…? and How many…? about food.","I can ask \"How much flour do we need?\" and \"How many eggs are there?\"","I can say \"There isn't much milk\" and \"We have a lot of rice.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام many مع المعدود وmuch مع غير المعدود في السؤال والنفي.","سيتمكن الطلاب من السؤال بـ How much وHow many عن الطعام.","أستطيع أن أسأل How much flour do we need? وHow many eggs are there?","أستطيع أن أقول There isn't much milk وWe have a lot of rice."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"salt","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sɔlt/","definition":"white grains that make food taste salty","arabic":"ملح","example":"Add a little salt to the soup.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS2-W01"},{"word":"butter","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbʌtɚ/","definition":"a soft yellow food made from milk","arabic":"زبدة","example":"Spread some butter on the bread.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS2-W02"},{"word":"oil","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɔɪl/","definition":"a liquid from plants, used for cooking","arabic":"زيت","example":"Fry the onions in olive oil.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS2-W03"},{"word":"onion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʌnjən/","definition":"a round vegetable with a strong taste and smell","arabic":"بصل","example":"Chopping onions makes me cry!","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use How many + plural countable noun: How many eggs do we need? Use How much + uncountable noun: How much flour do we need?\nIn negatives and questions, use many (countable) and much (uncountable): There aren't many apples. Is there much sugar? In positive sentences, we usually say a lot of for both: We have a lot of rice / a lot of eggs.\na few (countable) and a little (uncountable) mean a small number or amount: a few onions, a little salt.","examples":["How many onions are in the bag?","How much water should I add?","There isn't much time before dinner.","We don't have many plates.","My uncle eats a lot of dates.","Add a little garlic to the sauce.","There are a few lemons on the tree.","There's a lot of rice in the big pot."],"common_errors":["✗ How much eggs do we need? → ✓ How many eggs do we need? (eggs are countable → many.)","✗ There isn't many milk. → ✓ There isn't much milk. (milk is uncountable → much.)","✗ We have a lot rice. → ✓ We have a lot of rice. (a lot of.)","✗ Add a few salt. → ✓ Add a little salt. (uncountable → a little.)"],"arabic":"How many مع الأسماء المعدودة: How many eggs? وHow much مع غير المعدودة: How much flour?\nmany للمعدود وmuch لغير المعدود في النفي والسؤال، وa lot of للإثبات مع النوعين.\na few للمعدود (قليل من) وa little لغير المعدود.\nلا تنسَ of في a lot of."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “How Much Sugar? How Many Eggs? much, many, a lot of”. Let’s learn much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U6-LS2 | How Much Sugar? How Many Eggs? much, many, a lot of","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: We have a lot of flour. • There are a lot of dates. • Add a little salt and a few olives. There isn't much milk. • There aren't many eggs. How much honey is there? • How many spoons do we need? • Is there much oil?","on_screen":"We have a lot of flour. • There are a lot of dates. • Add a little salt and a few olives. | There isn't much milk. • There aren't many eggs. | How much honey is there? • How many spoons do we need? • Is there much oil?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use How many + plural countable noun: How many eggs do we need? Use How much + uncountable noun: How much flour do we need? In negatives and questions, use many (countable) and much (uncountable): There aren't many apples. Is there much sugar? In positive sentences, we usually say a lot of for both: We have a lot of rice / a lot of eggs.","on_screen":"much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. How many onions are in the bag? How much water should I add? There isn't much time before dinner.","on_screen":"How many onions are in the bag? / How much water should I add? / There isn't much time before dinner.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “How much eggs do we need?.” That’s not right. We say: “How many eggs do we need?.” eggs are countable → many.","on_screen":"✗ How much eggs do we need?   ✓ How many eggs do we need?","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"eggs\" – How much or How many? … Think! … *How many*. Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"How much flour do we need?\" and \"How many eggs are there?\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can ask \"How much flour do we need?\" and \"How many eggs are there?\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","How many مع الأسماء المعدودة: How many eggs? وHow much مع غير المعدودة: How much flour?","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: How much eggs do we need? — الصحيح: How many eggs do we need?","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أسأل How much flour do we need? وHow many eggs are there?"]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"How ___ eggs do we need?","options":["much","little","many","lot"],"answer":"many","explanation":"Countable → many / How many / a few.","explanation_ar":"المعدود ← many."},{"q":"How ___ butter is in the fridge?","options":["many","few","much","lot"],"answer":"much","explanation":"Uncountable → much / How much / a little.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود ← much."},{"q":"There isn't ___ salt in this soup.","options":["a few","much","lot","many"],"answer":"much","explanation":"Uncountable → much / How much / a little.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود ← much."},{"q":"We don't have ___ potatoes.","options":["many","lot","much","a little"],"answer":"many","explanation":"Countable → many / How many / a few.","explanation_ar":"المعدود ← many."},{"q":"My grandma makes ___ bread on Fridays.","options":["much of","many","a lot","a lot of"],"answer":"a lot of","explanation":"Positive sentences → a lot of (with of).","explanation_ar":"الإثبات ← a lot of."},{"q":"Add ___ sugar to the tea.","options":["a little","many","lot","a few"],"answer":"a little","explanation":"a few (countable) • a little (uncountable).","explanation_ar":"a few للمعدود وa little لغير المعدود."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write How much or How many. Word bank: How much, How many","items":[{"q":"______ onions are in the basket?","options":[],"answer":"How many","explanation":"Countable → many / How many / a few.","explanation_ar":"المعدود ← many."},{"q":"______ oil do I need?","options":[],"answer":"How much","explanation":"Uncountable → much / How much / a little.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود ← much."},{"q":"______ cups of flour are in the recipe?","options":[],"answer":"How many","explanation":"Countable → many / How many / a few.","explanation_ar":"المعدود ← many."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the mistake.","items":[{"q":"There aren't much cookies left.","options":[],"answer":"There aren't many cookies left.","explanation":"much → many. Countable → many / How many / a few.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: much → many. المعدود ← many."},{"q":"We have a lot honey.","options":[],"answer":"We have a lot of honey.","explanation":"a lot → a lot of. Positive sentences → a lot of (with of).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: a lot → a lot of. الإثبات ← a lot of."},{"q":"Put a few butter in the pan.","options":[],"answer":"Put a little butter in the pan.","explanation":"a few → a little. a few (countable) • a little (uncountable).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: a few → a little. a few للمعدود وa little لغير المعدود."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Answer about your food at home.","items":[{"q":"How many eggs do you eat in a week?","options":[],"answer":"I eat about five eggs a week.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How much water do you drink every day?","options":[],"answer":"I drink six glasses of water.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Does your family eat a lot of rice?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, we eat a lot of rice.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How many people eat dinner at your house?","options":[],"answer":"Seven people eat dinner at my house.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Is there much sugar in your favorite drink?","options":[],"answer":"No, there isn't much sugar in it.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Kitchen quiz.","items":[{"q":"Write 3 How much…? and 3 How many…? questions about a kitchen.","options":[],"answer":"How much milk is there? How much rice is there? How much honey is there? How many apples are there? How many cups are there? How many spoons are there?","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Answer 2 questions with a lot of / not much / not many.","options":[],"answer":"There's a lot of rice. There aren't many apples.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with a few and one with a little.","options":[],"answer":"We have a few lemons. Add a little honey.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Sentence Builder Race","mechanic":"sentence_builder","rules":["Each team receives the same tile set.","In 5 minutes, build as many different correct sentences as possible using much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few.","Write each sentence on the team sheet.","Swap sheets with another team to check. One point per correct sentence; no points for repeats."],"data":[{"cue":"How much / sugar / ?"},{"cue":"How many / eggs / ?"},{"cue":"there / any milk / –"},{"cue":"we / a lot of / rice / +"},{"cue":"How much / water / ?"},{"cue":"there / many / apples / –"},{"cue":"How many / onions / ?"},{"cue":"I / some / honey / +"},{"cue":"we / much / time / –"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"How ___ cups of tea do you drink?","options":["much","few","many","lot"],"answer":"many","explanation":"Countable → many / How many / a few.","explanation_ar":"المعدود ← many."},{"q":"How ___ milk do we need for the cake?","options":["many","much","lot","few"],"answer":"much","explanation":"Uncountable → much / How much / a little.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود ← much."},{"q":"","options":["There isn't a few flour left.","There isn't much flour left.","There aren't much flour left.","There isn't many flour left."],"answer":"There isn't much flour left.","explanation":"Uncountable → much / How much / a little.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود ← much."},{"q":"","options":["There aren't many tomatoes in the box.","There isn't many tomatoes in the box.","There aren't much tomatoes in the box.","There aren't a little tomatoes in the box."],"answer":"There aren't many tomatoes in the box.","explanation":"Countable → many / How many / a few.","explanation_ar":"المعدود ← many."},{"q":"Our neighbors grow ___ mint in their garden.","options":["much of","many of","a lot of","a lot"],"answer":"a lot of","explanation":"Positive sentences → a lot of (with of).","explanation_ar":"الإثبات ← a lot of."},{"q":"Add ___ olives to the salad.","options":["a little","much","lot","a few"],"answer":"a few","explanation":"a few (countable) • a little (uncountable).","explanation_ar":"a few للمعدود وa little لغير المعدود."},{"q":"","options":["How much juice is in the bottle?","How much juice are in the bottle?","How much juices is in the bottle?","How many juice is in the bottle?"],"answer":"How much juice is in the bottle?","explanation":"Uncountable → much / How much / a little.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود ← much."},{"q":"Put ___ salt on the eggs. Not too much!","options":["lots","a few","many","a little"],"answer":"a little","explanation":"a few (countable) • a little (uncountable).","explanation_ar":"a few للمعدود وa little لغير المعدود."},{"q":"Is there ___ honey in the jar? – No, not much.","options":["lot","many","a few","much"],"answer":"much","explanation":"Uncountable → much / How much / a little.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود ← much."},{"q":"","options":["We need much potatoes for the party.","We need a lot potatoes for the party.","We need a lot of potatoes for the party.","We need a little potatoes for the party."],"answer":"We need a lot of potatoes for the party.","explanation":"Positive sentences → a lot of (with of).","explanation_ar":"الإثبات ← a lot of."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"A kitchen counter with measuring cups, a recipe card, a few eggs in a bowl, a little milk in a glass and a big bag of rice labeled \"a lot\". Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A kitchen counter with measuring cups, a recipe card, a few eggs in a bowl, a little milk in a glass and a big bag of rice labeled \"a lot\""},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Let's Cook!”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of much / many / a lot of"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows salt (white grains that make food taste salty); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing salt: white grains that make food taste salty"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows butter (a soft yellow food made from milk); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing butter: a soft yellow food made from milk"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows oil (a liquid from plants, used for cooking); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing oil: a liquid from plants, used for cooking"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows onion (a round vegetable with a strong taste and smell); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing onion: a round vegetable with a strong taste and smell"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Sentence Builder Race”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Sentence Builder Race"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS2-W01","script":"salt. salt. Add a little salt to the soup.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS2-W02","script":"butter. butter. Spread some butter on the bread.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS2-W03","script":"oil. oil. Fry the onions in olive oil.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS2-W04","script":"onion. onion. Chopping onions makes me cry!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “How Much Sugar? How Many Eggs? much, many, a lot of”. Let’s learn much / many / a lot of; How much…? / How many…?; a little / a few together. Remember these patterns: We have a lot of flour. • There are a lot of dates. • Add a little salt and a few olives. There isn't much milk. • There aren't many eggs. How much honey is there? • How many spoons do we need? • Is there much oil? Use How many + plural countable noun: How many eggs do we need? Use How much + uncountable noun: How much flour do we need? In negatives and questions, use many (countable) and much (uncountable): There aren't many apples. Is there much sugar? In positive sentences, we usually say a lot of for both: We have a lot of rice / a lot of eggs. Here are some examples. How many onions are in the bag? How much water should I add? There isn't much time before dinner. Be careful! Some learners say: “How much eggs do we need?.” That’s not right. We say: “How many eggs do we need?.” eggs are countable → many. Quick check: \"eggs\" – How much or How many? … Think! … *How many*. Great job! Now you can say: I can ask \"How much flour do we need?\" and \"How many eggs are there?\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3","title":"A Jar of Honey, a Loaf of Bread: Containers and Cooking Words","objectives":["Students will be able to count uncountable food with container and quantity phrases.","Students will be able to use cooking verbs (mix, chop, boil, bake, fry, pour) in instructions.","I can say \"a jar of honey\" and \"two bottles of water\".","I can use cooking words like chop, mix and bake."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من عدّ الأطعمة غير المعدودة باستخدام عبارات الأوعية والكميات.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام أفعال الطبخ في التعليمات.","أستطيع أن أقول a jar of honey وtwo bottles of water.","أستطيع أن أستخدم كلمات الطبخ مثل chop وmix وbake."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"garlic","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡɑrlɪk/","definition":"a small, strong-smelling vegetable used for flavor","arabic":"ثوم","example":"This sauce has a lot of garlic.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-W01"},{"word":"honey","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhʌni/","definition":"a sweet, thick food made by bees","arabic":"عسل","example":"Honey from Al-Baha is famous.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-W02"},{"word":"bowl","pos":"noun","ipa":"/boʊl/","definition":"a round, deep dish for mixing or eating","arabic":"وعاء / زبدية","example":"Mix the eggs in a big bowl.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-W03"},{"word":"spoon","pos":"noun","ipa":"/spun/","definition":"a small tool for stirring and eating","arabic":"ملعقة","example":"Stir the tea with a spoon.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-W04"},{"word":"mix","pos":"verb","ipa":"/mɪks/","definition":"to put things together and stir them","arabic":"يخلط","example":"Mix the flour and the butter.","image_id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-W05"}],"explanation":{"text":"We can count uncountable food with a container or a quantity word: a bottle of water, a bag of rice, a jar of honey, a carton of milk, a can of tomatoes, a loaf of bread, a piece of cake, a cup of tea, a slice of cheese, a teaspoon of salt.\nTo make it plural, change the container: two bottles of water, three bags of rice (NOT two bottle of waters).\nCooking verbs: chop (cut into small pieces), mix (put together), boil (cook in very hot water), bake (cook in an oven), fry (cook in hot oil), pour (make a liquid go into something).\nCollocations/phrases: a bottle of water/oil • a bag of rice/flour • a jar of honey/jam • a carton of milk/juice • a can of tomatoes | a loaf of bread • a piece of cake • a slice of cheese • a cup of tea • a teaspoon of salt | chop • mix • boil • bake • fry • pour • stir • add","examples":["Can you buy a bottle of oil, please?","We need two bags of flour.","Grandpa brought a jar of honey from Al-Baha.","I'd like a piece of cake.","Chop the onions into small pieces.","Boil the water before you add the rice.","Bake the cookies for fifteen minutes.","Pour the milk into the bowl and mix well."],"common_errors":["✗ two bottle of waters → ✓ two bottles of water (Make the container plural, not the food.)","✗ a bread → ✓ a loaf of bread (Use a quantity word with uncountable food.)","✗ Cook the cake in the oven. → ✓ Bake the cake in the oven. (We bake cakes and bread.)","✗ a cup of a tea → ✓ a cup of tea (No a before the uncountable food.)"],"arabic":"نعدّ الأطعمة غير المعدودة بعبارات مثل: a bottle of water (زجاجة ماء) وa bag of rice (كيس أرز) وa loaf of bread (رغيف خبز).\nفي الجمع نجمع الوعاء وليس الطعام: two bottles of water.\nأفعال الطبخ: chop (يقطّع) وmix (يخلط) وboil (يغلي) وbake (يخبز) وfry (يقلي) وpour (يصب)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Jar of Honey, a Loaf of Bread: Containers and Cooking Words”. Let’s learn containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U6-LS3 | A Jar of Honey, a Loaf of Bread: Containers and Cooking Words","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. garlic: a small, strong-smelling vegetable used for flavor. honey: a sweet, thick food made by bees. bowl: a round, deep dish for mixing or eating.","on_screen":"garlic | honey | bowl","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We can count uncountable food with a container or a quantity word: a bottle of water, a bag of rice, a jar of honey, a carton of milk, a can of tomatoes, a loaf of bread, a piece of cake, a cup of tea, a slice of cheese, a teaspoon of salt. To make it plural, change the container: two bottles of water, three bags of rice (NOT two bottle of waters).","on_screen":"containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Can you buy a bottle of oil, please? We need two bags of flour. Grandpa brought a jar of honey from Al-Baha.","on_screen":"Can you buy a bottle of oil, please? / We need two bags of flour. / Grandpa brought a jar of honey from Al-Baha.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “two bottle of waters.” That’s not right. We say: “two bottles of water.” Make the container plural, not the food.","on_screen":"✗ two bottle of waters   ✓ two bottles of water","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Do we say \"two bottles of water\" or \"two bottle of waters\"? … Think! … *two bottles of water*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"a jar of honey\" and \"two bottles of water\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"a jar of honey\" and \"two bottles of water\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نعدّ الأطعمة غير المعدودة بعبارات مثل: a bottle of water (زجاجة ماء) وa bag of rice (كيس أرز) وa loaf of bread (رغيف خبز).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: two bottle of waters — الصحيح: two bottles of water","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول a jar of honey وtwo bottles of water."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"a ___ of honey","options":["slice","piece","loaf","jar"],"answer":"jar","explanation":"Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"a ___ of bread","options":["can","jar","bottle","loaf"],"answer":"loaf","explanation":"Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"two ___ of milk","options":["cartones","cartonss","cartons","carton"],"answer":"cartons","explanation":"Make the container plural, not the food.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الوعاء لا الطعام."},{"q":"___ the carrots into small pieces.","options":["Chop","Pour","Boil","Bake"],"answer":"Chop","explanation":"Choose the cooking verb that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر فعل الطبخ المناسب."},{"q":"___ the bread in a hot oven.","options":["Chop","Bake","Fry","Pour"],"answer":"Bake","explanation":"Choose the cooking verb that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر فعل الطبخ المناسب."},{"q":"Stir the soup with a ___.","options":["carton","jar","spoon","bowl"],"answer":"spoon","explanation":"Choose the kitchen word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المطبخ المناسبة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the container to the food.","items":[{"q":"a bottle of","options":["cheese","water","tea","tomatoes","rice","salt"],"answer":"water","explanation":"a bottle of → water. Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"a bag of","options":["cheese","water","tea","tomatoes","rice","salt"],"answer":"rice","explanation":"a bag of → rice. Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"a can of","options":["cheese","water","tea","tomatoes","rice","salt"],"answer":"tomatoes","explanation":"a can of → tomatoes. Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"a slice of","options":["cheese","water","tea","tomatoes","rice","salt"],"answer":"cheese","explanation":"a slice of → cheese. Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"a cup of","options":["cheese","water","tea","tomatoes","rice","salt"],"answer":"tea","explanation":"a cup of → tea. Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"a teaspoon of","options":["cheese","water","tea","tomatoes","rice","salt"],"answer":"salt","explanation":"a teaspoon of → salt. Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write a shopping list with containers.","items":[{"q":"two ___ of ___","options":[],"answer":"two bottles of water","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"a ___ of ___","options":[],"answer":"a loaf of bread","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"three ___ of ___","options":[],"answer":"three cans of beans","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"a ___ of juice","options":[],"answer":"a carton of juice","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In my family, we often ___ (a cooking verb) chicken.","options":[],"answer":"In my family, we often fry chicken.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Cooking show.","items":[{"q":"Act out 4 cooking verbs. Your team guesses. Write them.","options":[],"answer":"chop, mix, pour, fry","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 instructions for making tea.","options":[],"answer":"Boil the water. Pour it into a cup. Add a little sugar.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your family's shopping list with 5 container phrases.","options":[],"answer":"a bag of flour, a carton of milk, two jars of jam, a bottle of oil, a loaf of bread","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Memory Match","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Place all cards face down in a grid.","Turn over two cards. If the word matches its definition, keep the pair and say a sentence with the word.","If not, turn them back over; the next player plays.","The player with the most pairs wins."],"data":[{"word":"recipe","match":"instructions that tell you how to cook something","arabic":"وصفة طعام"},{"word":"ingredient","match":"one of the foods you use to make a dish","arabic":"مكوّن"},{"word":"flour","match":"white or brown powder from wheat, used to make bread and cakes","arabic":"دقيق / طحين"},{"word":"sugar","match":"a sweet white or brown food you add to drinks and cakes","arabic":"سكر"},{"word":"salt","match":"white grains that make food taste salty","arabic":"ملح"},{"word":"butter","match":"a soft yellow food made from milk","arabic":"زبدة"},{"word":"oil","match":"a liquid from plants, used for cooking","arabic":"زيت"},{"word":"onion","match":"a round vegetable with a strong taste and smell","arabic":"بصل"},{"word":"garlic","match":"a small, strong-smelling vegetable used for flavor","arabic":"ثوم"},{"word":"honey","match":"a sweet, thick food made by bees","arabic":"عسل"},{"word":"bowl","match":"a round, deep dish for mixing or eating","arabic":"وعاء / زبدية"},{"word":"spoon","match":"a small tool for stirring and eating","arabic":"ملعقة"},{"word":"mix","match":"to put things together and stir them","arabic":"يخلط"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"a ___ of oil","options":["loaf","bottle","slice","piece"],"answer":"bottle","explanation":"Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"a ___ of cake","options":["piece","carton","jar","bottle"],"answer":"piece","explanation":"Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"three ___ of rice","options":["bags","bages","bag","bagss"],"answer":"bags","explanation":"Make the container plural, not the food.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الوعاء لا الطعام."},{"q":"___ the eggs in hot water for ten minutes.","options":["Chop","Fry it","Bake","Boil"],"answer":"Boil","explanation":"Choose the cooking verb that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر فعل الطبخ المناسب."},{"q":"___ the juice into the glasses.","options":["Bake","Chop","Pour","Fry"],"answer":"Pour","explanation":"Choose the cooking verb that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر فعل الطبخ المناسب."},{"q":"","options":["Can I have a cup tea?","Can I have a cup of a tea?","Can I have a cups of tea?","Can I have a cup of tea?"],"answer":"Can I have a cup of tea?","explanation":"Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"We mix the cake in a big ___.","options":["spoon","bowl","can","jar"],"answer":"bowl","explanation":"Choose the kitchen word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المطبخ المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["Buy two loafs of bread.","Buy two loaf of breads.","Buy two loaves of bread.","Buy two breads."],"answer":"Buy two loaves of bread.","explanation":"Make the container plural, not the food.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الوعاء لا الطعام."},{"q":"___ the onions in a little oil.","options":["Fry","Boil the","Pour","Bake"],"answer":"Fry","explanation":"Choose the cooking verb that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر فعل الطبخ المناسب."},{"q":"Which is a container?","options":["loaf","carton","teaspoon","slice"],"answer":"carton","explanation":"Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A pantry shelf with labeled containers – a jar of honey, a bottle of oil, a bag of rice, a carton of milk, a can of tomatoes, a loaf of bread – and icons of cooking actions. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A pantry shelf with labeled containers – a jar of honey, a bottle of oil, a bag of rice, a carton of milk, a can of tomatoes, a loaf of bread – and icons of cooking actions"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows garlic (a small, strong-smelling vegetable used for flavor); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing garlic: a small, strong-smelling vegetable used for flavor"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows honey (a sweet, thick food made by bees); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing honey: a sweet, thick food made by bees"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows bowl (a round, deep dish for mixing or eating); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing bowl: a round, deep dish for mixing or eating"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows spoon (a small tool for stirring and eating); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing spoon: a small tool for stirring and eating"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows mix (to put things together and stir them); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing mix: to put things together and stir them"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Memory Match”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Memory Match"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-W01","script":"garlic. garlic. This sauce has a lot of garlic.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-W02","script":"honey. honey. Honey from Al-Baha is famous.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-W03","script":"bowl. bowl. Mix the eggs in a big bowl.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-W04","script":"spoon. spoon. Stir the tea with a spoon.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-W05","script":"mix. mix. Mix the flour and the butter.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “A Jar of Honey, a Loaf of Bread: Containers and Cooking Words”. Let’s learn containers and quantity phrases (a bottle of, a bag of, a jar of, a loaf of, a piece of, a cup of); cooking verbs together. Meet some new words. garlic: a small, strong-smelling vegetable used for flavor. honey: a sweet, thick food made by bees. bowl: a round, deep dish for mixing or eating. We can count uncountable food with a container or a quantity word: a bottle of water, a bag of rice, a jar of honey, a carton of milk, a can of tomatoes, a loaf of bread, a piece of cake, a cup of tea, a slice of cheese, a teaspoon of salt. To make it plural, change the container: two bottles of water, three bags of rice (NOT two bottle of waters). Here are some examples. Can you buy a bottle of oil, please? We need two bags of flour. Grandpa brought a jar of honey from Al-Baha. Be careful! Some learners say: “two bottle of waters.” That’s not right. We say: “two bottles of water.” Make the container plural, not the food. Quick check: Do we say \"two bottles of water\" or \"two bottle of waters\"? … Think! … *two bottles of water*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"a jar of honey\" and \"two bottles of water\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS4","title":"Flour, Sugar, and Butter: Commas in a Series","objectives":["Students will be able to use commas to separate three or more words or phrases in a series.","Students will be able to punctuate lists of ingredients and recipe actions.","I can write \"We need flour, sugar, and two eggs.\"","I can write \"Chop, mix, and bake.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام الفواصل للفصل بين ثلاث كلمات أو عبارات أو أكثر.","سيتمكن الطلاب من ترقيم قوائم المكونات وخطوات الوصفة.","أستطيع أن أكتب We need flour, sugar, and two eggs.","أستطيع أن أكتب Chop, mix, and bake."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"recipe","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɛsəpi/","definition":"instructions that tell you how to cook something","arabic":"وصفة طعام","example":"Grandma's recipe for date cookies is a secret.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ingredient","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈɡridiənt/","definition":"one of the foods you use to make a dish","arabic":"مكوّن","example":"Flour is the main ingredient in bread.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"flour","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈflaʊɚ/","definition":"white or brown powder from wheat, used to make bread and cakes","arabic":"دقيق / طحين","example":"We need two cups of flour.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sugar","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʃʊɡɚ/","definition":"a sweet white or brown food you add to drinks and cakes","arabic":"سكر","example":"Don't put too much sugar in your tea.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"salt","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sɔlt/","definition":"white grains that make food taste salty","arabic":"ملح","example":"Add a little salt to the soup.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"butter","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbʌtɚ/","definition":"a soft yellow food made from milk","arabic":"زبدة","example":"Spread some butter on the bread.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A series is a list of three or more things. Put a comma after each item, and and (or or) before the last one: We need flour, sugar, and butter.\nThe items can be phrases: We need a bag of flour, a jar of honey, and two cartons of milk. They can be actions: Chop the onions, fry them, and add the rice.\nIn this programme we use the comma before and in a series (the American \"serial comma\"). With only two items, don't use a comma: salt and pepper.\nthree or more items → comma after each item before and/or\nitems can be words, phrases or actions\ntwo items → no comma: bread and cheese\nDon't put a comma after the last item or before the first.","examples":["We need eggs, milk, and flour.","Add a cup of rice, two cups of water, and a little salt.","Wash the vegetables, chop them, and put them in a bowl.","Would you like tea, coffee, or juice?","My grandma's kitchen has a big oven, an old table, and many jars.","I like apples and grapes.","Lina, Sara, and Noura baked the cake together.","Mix the butter, add the sugar, and stir well."],"common_errors":["✗ We need, flour, sugar, and eggs. → ✓ We need flour, sugar, and eggs. (No comma before the first item.)","✗ Chop the onions fry them and add salt. → ✓ Chop the onions, fry them, and add salt. (Commas between actions in a series.)","✗ I like tea, and coffee. → ✓ I like tea and coffee. (Two items → no comma.)","✗ We need milk, eggs, butter, and. → ✓ We need milk, eggs, and butter. (and goes before the last item.)"],"arabic":"السلسلة: ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر، نضع فاصلة بعد كل عنصر وand أو or قبل الأخير.\nالعناصر قد تكون كلمات أو عبارات أو أفعالًا: Chop the onions, fry them, and add the rice.\nمع عنصرين فقط لا نضع فاصلة: bread and cheese.\nلا نضع فاصلة قبل العنصر الأول."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Flour, Sugar, and Butter: Commas in a Series”. Let’s learn commas in a series of words, phrases and actions together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U6-LS4 | Flour, Sugar, and Butter: Commas in a Series","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A series is a list of three or more things. Put a comma after each item, and and (or or) before the last one: We need flour, sugar, and butter.","on_screen":"commas in a series of words, phrases and actions","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A series is a list of three or more things. Put a comma after each item, and and (or or) before the last one: We need flour, sugar, and butter. The items can be phrases: We need a bag of flour, a jar of honey, and two cartons of milk. They can be actions: Chop the onions, fry them, and add the rice.","on_screen":"three or more items → comma after each item before and/or • items can be words, phrases or actions • two items → no comma: bread and cheese","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. We need eggs, milk, and flour. Add a cup of rice, two cups of water, and a little salt. Wash the vegetables, chop them, and put them in a bowl.","on_screen":"We need eggs, milk, and flour. / Add a cup of rice, two cups of water, and a little salt. / Wash the vegetables, chop them, and put them in a bowl.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “We need, flour, sugar, and eggs.” That’s not right. We say: “We need flour, sugar, and eggs.” No comma before the first item.","on_screen":"✗ We need, flour, sugar, and eggs.   ✓ We need flour, sugar, and eggs.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: How many items do we need to use commas in a series? … Think! … Three or more. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"We need flour, sugar, and two eggs.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"We need flour, sugar, and two eggs.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: commas in a series of words, phrases and actions.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","السلسلة: ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر، نضع فاصلة بعد كل عنصر وand أو or قبل الأخير.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: We need, flour, sugar, and eggs. — الصحيح: We need flour, sugar, and eggs.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب We need flour, sugar, and two eggs."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Mint Tea (editing passage)","body":"You need water green tea fresh mint, and a little sugar. Boil the water add the tea, and wait three minutes. Put the mint, and the sugar in a teapot. Pour the tea stir it, and enjoy!","word_count":37,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["We need onions, garlic, tomatoes and.","We need, onions, garlic, and tomatoes.","We need onions garlic and tomatoes.","We need onions, garlic, and tomatoes."],"answer":"We need onions, garlic, and tomatoes.","explanation":"Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["Wash, the rice boil the water and add the salt.","Wash the rice boil the water and add the salt.","Wash the rice, boil the water, and add the salt.","Wash the rice, boil the water, add the salt and."],"answer":"Wash the rice, boil the water, and add the salt.","explanation":"Phrases and actions in a series also need commas.","explanation_ar":"العبارات والأفعال تحتاج فواصل أيضًا."},{"q":"","options":["I'd like bread, butter.","I'd like bread and butter.","I'd like bread, and butter.","I'd like, bread and butter."],"answer":"I'd like bread and butter.","explanation":"Two items → no comma.","explanation_ar":"عنصران ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Do you want tea coffee or milk?","Do you want, tea, coffee or milk?","Do you want tea, coffee, or milk?","Do you want tea, coffee, milk, or?"],"answer":"Do you want tea, coffee, or milk?","explanation":"Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["Buy a bag, of rice a bottle of oil, and a jar of jam.","Buy a bag of rice a bottle of oil and a jar of jam.","Buy, a bag of rice, a bottle of oil, and a jar of jam.","Buy a bag of rice, a bottle of oil, and a jar of jam."],"answer":"Buy a bag of rice, a bottle of oil, and a jar of jam.","explanation":"Phrases and actions in a series also need commas.","explanation_ar":"العبارات والأفعال تحتاج فواصل أيضًا."},{"q":"","options":["Hamad, Ziyad, and Rakan cooked lunch.","Hamad Ziyad and Rakan cooked lunch.","Hamad, Ziyad, and, Rakan cooked lunch.",", Hamad, Ziyad and Rakan cooked lunch."],"answer":"Hamad, Ziyad, and Rakan cooked lunch.","explanation":"No comma before the first item.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة قبل العنصر الأول."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add or remove commas.","items":[{"q":"Mix the flour the sugar, and the butter.","options":[],"answer":"Mix the flour, the sugar, and the butter.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"Chop the garlic, fry it and add the sauce.","options":[],"answer":"Chop the garlic, fry it, and add the sauce.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Phrases and actions in a series also need commas.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. العبارات والأفعال تحتاج فواصل أيضًا."},{"q":"We need salt, and pepper.","options":[],"answer":"We need salt and pepper.","explanation":", → (delete). Two items → no comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). عنصران ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"I bought milk, eggs and cheese.","options":[],"answer":"I bought milk, eggs, and cheese.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"We need, apples, pears, and bananas.","options":[],"answer":"We need apples, pears, and bananas.","explanation":", → (delete). No comma before the first item.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). لا فاصلة قبل العنصر الأول."},{"q":"Pour the milk add the honey, and stir.","options":[],"answer":"Pour the milk, add the honey, and stir.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Phrases and actions in a series also need commas.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. العبارات والأفعال تحتاج فواصل أيضًا."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the recipe.","items":[{"q":"You need water green tea fresh mint, and a little sugar.","options":[],"answer":"You need water, green tea, fresh mint, and a little sugar.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"You need water green tea fresh mint, and a little sugar.","options":[],"answer":"You need water, green tea, fresh mint, and a little sugar.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"You need water green tea fresh mint, and a little sugar.","options":[],"answer":"You need water, green tea, fresh mint, and a little sugar.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"Put the mint, and the sugar in a teapot.","options":[],"answer":"Put the mint and the sugar in a teapot.","explanation":", → (delete). Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"You need water green tea fresh mint, and a little sugar.","options":[],"answer":"You need water, green tea, fresh mint, and a little sugar.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write series sentences.","items":[{"q":"Write the ingredients for your favorite sandwich in one sentence.","options":[],"answer":"I need bread, cheese, and tomatoes.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas in a series of words, phrases and actions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 steps for washing your hands in one sentence with commas.","options":[],"answer":"Wet your hands, use soap, and rinse them well.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas in a series of words, phrases and actions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with only two items (no comma).","options":[],"answer":"I like milk and honey.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses commas in a series of words, phrases and actions correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spelling Relay","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["Teams line up facing the board.","The teacher says a word; the first student runs to the board and writes the first letter.","The next student adds the next letter, and so on.","The first team with the correct spelling wins the point."],"data":[{"word":"recipe","clue":"instructions that tell you how to cook something"},{"word":"ingredient","clue":"one of the foods you use to make a dish"},{"word":"flour","clue":"white or brown powder from wheat, used to make bread and cakes"},{"word":"butter","clue":"a soft yellow food made from milk"},{"word":"onion","clue":"a round vegetable with a strong taste and smell"},{"word":"garlic","clue":"a small, strong-smelling vegetable used for flavor"},{"word":"sugar","clue":"a sweet white or brown food you add to drinks and cakes"},{"word":"salt","clue":"white grains that make food taste salty"},{"word":"oil","clue":"a liquid from plants, used for cooking"},{"word":"honey","clue":"a sweet, thick food made by bees"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["Add, salt, pepper, and lemon juice.","Add salt pepper and lemon juice.","Add salt, pepper, and lemon juice.","Add salt, pepper, lemon juice and."],"answer":"Add salt, pepper, and lemon juice.","explanation":"Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"How many commas? \"We need eggs flour and milk.\"","options":["0","2","1","3"],"answer":"2","explanation":"Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["Peel, the potatoes cut them, and boil them.","Peel the potatoes cut them and boil them.","Peel the potatoes, cut them, boil them and.","Peel the potatoes, cut them, and boil them."],"answer":"Peel the potatoes, cut them, and boil them.","explanation":"Phrases and actions in a series also need commas.","explanation_ar":"العبارات والأفعال تحتاج فواصل أيضًا."},{"q":"","options":["We had rice, and chicken for lunch.","We had rice and chicken for lunch.","We had rice, chicken, for lunch.","We had, rice and chicken for lunch."],"answer":"We had rice and chicken for lunch.","explanation":"Two items → no comma.","explanation_ar":"عنصران ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"Where is the missing comma? \"I bought a cake, some cookies and a pie.\"","options":["after \"pie\"","after \"a\"","after \"cookies\"","after \"bought\""],"answer":"after \"cookies\"","explanation":"Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["Would you like water, juice, or milk?","Would you like water, juice, milk or.","Would you like, water, juice, or milk?","Would you like water juice or milk?"],"answer":"Would you like water, juice, or milk?","explanation":"Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["My aunt, my uncle, and my cousins came for dinner.","My aunt my uncle and my cousins came for dinner.","My aunt, my uncle, and, my cousins came for dinner.",", My aunt my uncle and my cousins came for dinner."],"answer":"My aunt, my uncle, and my cousins came for dinner.","explanation":"No comma before the first item.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة قبل العنصر الأول."},{"q":"Which list needs no comma?","options":["bread, jam, and honey","eggs, milk, and flour","rice, chicken, and salad","bread and jam"],"answer":"bread and jam","explanation":"Two items → no comma.","explanation_ar":"عنصران ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["Cut, the bread, spread the butter and add the cheese.","Cut the bread, spread the butter, add the cheese and.","Cut the bread, spread the butter, and add the cheese.","Cut the bread spread the butter and add the cheese."],"answer":"Cut the bread, spread the butter, and add the cheese.","explanation":"Phrases and actions in a series also need commas.","explanation_ar":"العبارات والأفعال تحتاج فواصل أيضًا."},{"q":"","options":["The shop sells bags of flour, jars of honey, bottles of oil and.","The shop sells bags of flour jars of honey and bottles of oil.","The shop sells, bags of flour, jars of honey, and bottles of oil.","The shop sells bags of flour, jars of honey, and bottles of oil."],"answer":"The shop sells bags of flour, jars of honey, and bottles of oil.","explanation":"Phrases and actions in a series also need commas.","explanation_ar":"العبارات والأفعال تحتاج فواصل أيضًا."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Let's Cook!” that shows commas in a series of words, phrases and actions in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Let's Cook!” that shows commas in a series of words, phrases and actions in action"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spelling Relay”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spelling Relay"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Flour, Sugar, and Butter: Commas in a Series”. Let’s learn commas in a series of words, phrases and actions together. A series is a list of three or more things. Put a comma after each item, and and (or or) before the last one: We need flour, sugar, and butter. A series is a list of three or more things. Put a comma after each item, and and (or or) before the last one: We need flour, sugar, and butter. The items can be phrases: We need a bag of flour, a jar of honey, and two cartons of milk. They can be actions: Chop the onions, fry them, and add the rice. Here are some examples. We need eggs, milk, and flour. Add a cup of rice, two cups of water, and a little salt. Wash the vegetables, chop them, and put them in a bowl. Be careful! Some learners say: “We need, flour, sugar, and eggs.” That’s not right. We say: “We need flour, sugar, and eggs.” No comma before the first item. Quick check: How many items do we need to use commas in a series? … Think! … Three or more. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"We need flour, sugar, and two eggs.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS5","title":"Our Class Cookbook: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to talk about the ingredients and amounts in a recipe.","Students will be able to write a simple recipe with quantities, imperatives and commas in a series.","I can explain a recipe to my group.","I can write a recipe for our class cookbook."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من التحدث عن مكونات وصفة وكمياتها.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة وصفة بسيطة مع الكميات وصيغة الأمر والفواصل.","أستطيع أن أشرح وصفة لمجموعتي.","أستطيع أن أكتب وصفة لكتاب الطبخ الخاص بالصف."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"recipe","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈrɛsəpi/","definition":"instructions that tell you how to cook something","arabic":"وصفة طعام","example":"Grandma's recipe for date cookies is a secret.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"ingredient","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈɡridiənt/","definition":"one of the foods you use to make a dish","arabic":"مكوّن","example":"Flour is the main ingredient in bread.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"flour","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈflaʊɚ/","definition":"white or brown powder from wheat, used to make bread and cakes","arabic":"دقيق / طحين","example":"We need two cups of flour.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"sugar","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʃʊɡɚ/","definition":"a sweet white or brown food you add to drinks and cakes","arabic":"سكر","example":"Don't put too much sugar in your tea.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"salt","pos":"noun","ipa":"/sɔlt/","definition":"white grains that make food taste salty","arabic":"ملح","example":"Add a little salt to the soup.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"butter","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbʌtɚ/","definition":"a soft yellow food made from milk","arabic":"زبدة","example":"Spread some butter on the bread.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"oil","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ɔɪl/","definition":"a liquid from plants, used for cooking","arabic":"زيت","example":"Fry the onions in olive oil.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"onion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈʌnjən/","definition":"a round vegetable with a strong taste and smell","arabic":"بصل","example":"Chopping onions makes me cry!","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"garlic","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɡɑrlɪk/","definition":"a small, strong-smelling vegetable used for flavor","arabic":"ثوم","example":"This sauce has a lot of garlic.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"honey","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈhʌni/","definition":"a sweet, thick food made by bees","arabic":"عسل","example":"Honey from Al-Baha is famous.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"bowl","pos":"noun","ipa":"/boʊl/","definition":"a round, deep dish for mixing or eating","arabic":"وعاء / زبدية","example":"Mix the eggs in a big bowl.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"spoon","pos":"noun","ipa":"/spun/","definition":"a small tool for stirring and eating","arabic":"ملعقة","example":"Stir the tea with a spoon.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"mix","pos":"verb","ipa":"/mɪks/","definition":"to put things together and stir them","arabic":"يخلط","example":"Mix the flour and the butter.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 6: countable and uncountable nouns, some/any, much/many/a lot of, a few/a little, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series.\nA recipe has a title, a list of ingredients with amounts, and steps with imperative cooking verbs in order.\n✔ countable: a few strawberries • uncountable: a little honey\n✔ some (positive), any (negative/questions)\n✔ imperatives: wash, cut, mix, add, pour\n✔ commas in a series of items and steps","examples":["You need some flour, a few eggs, and a little milk.","Is there any honey in the jar?","There isn't much time, so let's start.","How many bananas do we need?","Pour a carton of milk into the bowl.","Chop the apples, mix them with yogurt, and add honey.","We need a lot of ice for the juice.","Don't add any salt to the fruit salad."],"common_errors":["✗ You need a honey. → ✓ You need some honey. (honey is uncountable.)","✗ How much bananas do we need? → ✓ How many bananas do we need? (countable → many.)","✗ Wash the fruit cut it and mix it. → ✓ Wash the fruit, cut it, and mix it. (Commas between steps.)"],"arabic":"نراجع المعدود وغير المعدود وsome وany وmuch وmany والأوعية وأفعال الطبخ والفواصل.\nالوصفة لها عنوان وقائمة مكونات بكمياتها وخطوات بصيغة الأمر.\nتذكّر: a few للمعدود وa little لغير المعدود."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Class Cookbook: Language in Use”. Let’s learn countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L03-U6-LS5 | Our Class Cookbook: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Cooking show: in groups, choose a simple dish. One student is the chef and explains: \"You need some…, a few…, a bottle of…\". The others ask \"How much…? How many…?\" and the chef answers.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 6: countable and uncountable nouns, some/any, much/many/a lot of, a few/a little, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series. A recipe has a title, a list of ingredients with amounts, and steps with imperative cooking verbs in order.","on_screen":"✔ countable: a few strawberries • uncountable: a little honey • ✔ some (positive), any (negative/questions) • ✔ imperatives: wash, cut, mix, add, pour","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. You need some flour, a few eggs, and a little milk. Is there any honey in the jar? There isn't much time, so let's start.","on_screen":"You need some flour, a few eggs, and a little milk. / Is there any honey in the jar? / There isn't much time, so let's start.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “You need a honey.” That’s not right. We say: “You need some honey.” honey is uncountable.","on_screen":"✗ You need a honey.   ✓ You need some honey.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “How much bananas do we need?”? … Think! … It should be “How many bananas do we need?”. Great job! Now you can say: I can explain a recipe to my group.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can explain a recipe to my group.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع المعدود وغير المعدود وsome وany وmuch وmany والأوعية وأفعال الطبخ والفواصل.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: You need a honey. — الصحيح: You need some honey.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أشرح وصفة لمجموعتي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"Fruit Salad with Honey – Lina","body":"You need: two bananas, an apple, a few strawberries, a cup of grapes, and a little honey.\nWash the fruit, cut it into small pieces, and put it in a big bowl.\nAdd some honey and a little lemon juice.\nMix everything gently with a spoon.\nDon't add any sugar – the fruit is sweet enough!\nPut the bowl in the fridge for ten minutes. Enjoy!","word_count":66,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Lina's recipe. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Lina's fruit salad has two bananas.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Fruit Salad with Honey – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"You need a lot of sugar.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Fruit Salad with Honey – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"You cut the fruit into small pieces.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Fruit Salad with Honey – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"You add some honey and a little lemon juice.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “Fruit Salad with Honey – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"You mix the fruit with a knife.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Fruit Salad with Honey – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The salad goes in the oven for ten minutes.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “Fruit Salad with Honey – Lina”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"You need ___ strawberries.","options":["a little","much","a few","any"],"answer":"a few","explanation":"Countable vs uncountable (a few / a little; many / much).","explanation_ar":"المعدود وغير المعدود."},{"q":"Don't add ___ sugar.","options":["some","a few","any","many"],"answer":"any","explanation":"some (positive) / any (negative and questions).","explanation_ar":"some وany."},{"q":"You need a ___ of grapes.","options":["cup","loaf","can","slice"],"answer":"cup","explanation":"Container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"الوعاء أو الكمية."},{"q":"___ everything gently with a spoon.","options":["Boil","Bake","Fry","Mix"],"answer":"Mix","explanation":"Imperative cooking verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل طبخ بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"","options":["Wash, the fruit cut it, and put it in a bowl.","Wash the fruit, cut it, and put it in a bowl.","Wash the fruit, cut it, put it in a bowl and.","Wash the fruit cut it and put it in a bowl."],"answer":"Wash the fruit, cut it, and put it in a bowl.","explanation":"Commas in a series.","explanation_ar":"الفواصل في السلسلة."},{"q":"How ___ honey do we need?","options":["much","lots","many","few"],"answer":"much","explanation":"Countable vs uncountable (a few / a little; many / much).","explanation_ar":"المعدود وغير المعدود."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Cooking show. Write the chef's answers.","items":[{"q":"How many eggs do we need?","options":[],"answer":"We need three eggs.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How much flour do we need?","options":[],"answer":"We need two cups of flour.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Is there any milk?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, there's a carton of milk in the fridge.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"What do we do first?","options":[],"answer":"First, mix the eggs and the milk in a bowl.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Do we need any sugar?","options":[],"answer":"Yes, a little sugar.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your recipe.","items":[{"q":"Plan: title, 5 ingredients with amounts, 3 steps.","options":[],"answer":"Cheese Toast: two slices of bread, two slices of cheese, a little butter, a tomato, some oregano. Steps: spread, add, bake","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your recipe (6–8 lines).","options":[],"answer":"Cheese Toast. You need two slices of bread, two slices of cheese, a little butter, and a tomato. Spread the butter on the bread. Add the cheese, the tomato, and some oregano. Bake it for five minutes. Enjoy!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: a few/a little? some/any? commas? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"a few butter\" to \"a little butter\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Board Race Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team stands at the board.","The teacher says a cue word and a task (meaning, spelling or sentence with countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review)).","The first correct answer wins a point; rotate players every round.","Play 10 rounds."],"data":[{"cue":"recipe","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"ingredient","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"flour","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"sugar","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"salt","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"butter","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"oil","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"onion","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"garlic","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"honey","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"bowl","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"spoon","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"mix","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"We need ___ potatoes for the soup.","options":["much","any","a few","a little"],"answer":"a few","explanation":"Countable vs uncountable (a few / a little; many / much).","explanation_ar":"المعدود وغير المعدود."},{"q":"There isn't ___ rice left. Let's buy some.","options":["some","a few","many","any"],"answer":"any","explanation":"some (positive) / any (negative and questions).","explanation_ar":"some وany."},{"q":"a ___ of jam","options":["slice","piece","jar","loaf"],"answer":"jar","explanation":"Container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"الوعاء أو الكمية."},{"q":"___ the chicken in the oven for one hour.","options":["Bake","Pour","Chop","Mix up"],"answer":"Bake","explanation":"Imperative cooking verb.","explanation_ar":"فعل طبخ بصيغة الأمر."},{"q":"","options":["Add the eggs, the milk, the sugar and.","Add the eggs, the milk, and the sugar.","Add the eggs the milk and the sugar.","Add, the eggs, the milk, and the sugar."],"answer":"Add the eggs, the milk, and the sugar.","explanation":"Commas in a series.","explanation_ar":"الفواصل في السلسلة."},{"q":"How ___ cookies did you bake?","options":["much","lot","little","many"],"answer":"many","explanation":"Countable vs uncountable (a few / a little; many / much).","explanation_ar":"المعدود وغير المعدود."},{"q":"","options":["Would you like a soup?","Would you like some soups?","Would you like some soup?","Would you like any soup?"],"answer":"Would you like some soup?","explanation":"some (positive) / any (negative and questions).","explanation_ar":"some وany."},{"q":"Buy two ___ of milk, please.","options":["cartons","cartones","cartons'","carton"],"answer":"cartons","explanation":"Container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"الوعاء أو الكمية."},{"q":"","options":["Don't add many salt.","Don't add any salt.","Don't add a salt.","Don't add some salt."],"answer":"Don't add any salt.","explanation":"some (positive) / any (negative and questions).","explanation_ar":"some وany."},{"q":"Pick the best first line for a recipe:","options":["You need some flour, a few eggs, and a little milk.","You need, some flour, a few eggs and a little milk.","You need some flours, a little eggs, and many milk.","You need a flour, a few eggs, and a little milks."],"answer":"You need some flour, a few eggs, and a little milk.","explanation":"Countable vs uncountable (a few / a little; many / much).","explanation_ar":"المعدود وغير المعدود."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"A class cookbook on a table open to a page with a drawing of a fruit salad, children around it holding bowls, spoons and fruit. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A class cookbook on a table open to a page with a drawing of a fruit salad, children around it holding bowls, spoons and fruit"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Let's Cook!”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Let's Cook!”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L03-U6-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Board Race Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Board Race Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS5-T1","script":"You need: two bananas, an apple, a few strawberries, a cup of grapes, and a little honey. Wash the fruit, cut it into small pieces, and put it in a big bowl. Add some honey and a little lemon juice. Mix everything gently with a spoon. Don't add any sugar – the fruit is sweet enough! Put the bowl in the fridge for ten minutes. Enjoy!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L03-U6-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Class Cookbook: Language in Use”. Let’s learn countable/uncountable, some/any, much/many/a lot of, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Cooking show: in groups, choose a simple dish. One student is the chef and explains: \"You need some…, a few…, a bottle of…\". The others ask \"How much…? How many…?\" and the chef answers. Today you use all of Unit 6: countable and uncountable nouns, some/any, much/many/a lot of, a few/a little, containers, cooking verbs and commas in a series. A recipe has a title, a list of ingredients with amounts, and steps with imperative cooking verbs in order. Here are some examples. You need some flour, a few eggs, and a little milk. Is there any honey in the jar? There isn't much time, so let's start. Be careful! Some learners say: “You need a honey.” That’s not right. We say: “You need some honey.” honey is uncountable. Quick check: what is wrong with “How much bananas do we need?”? … Think! … It should be “How many bananas do we need?”. Great job! Now you can say: I can explain a recipe to my group.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"There's ___ cheese on the plate.","options":["some","any","a","many"],"answer":"some","explanation":"some in positive sentences, offers and requests.","explanation_ar":"some للإثبات والعرض والطلب."},{"q":"Are there ___ bananas in the kitchen?","options":["a","much","any","some"],"answer":"any","explanation":"any in negatives and questions.","explanation_ar":"any للنفي والسؤال."},{"q":"","options":["I'd like any water, please.","I'd like a water, please.","I'd like some water, please.","I'd like some waters, please."],"answer":"I'd like some water, please.","explanation":"Uncountable: no a/an, no plural.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود: بدون a وبدون جمع."},{"q":"We need ___ orange for the juice.","options":["an","a","some","any"],"answer":"an","explanation":"Countable: a/an + singular, or a plural.","explanation_ar":"المعدود: مفرد مع a أو جمع."},{"q":"Find the uncountable noun.","options":["spoon","carrot","plate","rice"],"answer":"rice","explanation":"Uncountable: no a/an, no plural.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود: بدون a وبدون جمع."},{"q":"How ___ glasses of water do you drink?","options":["many","lot","much","few"],"answer":"many","explanation":"Countable → many / How many / a few.","explanation_ar":"المعدود ← many."},{"q":"How ___ oil do we need?","options":["few","much","lot","many"],"answer":"much","explanation":"Uncountable → much / How much / a little.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود ← much."},{"q":"","options":["There isn't a few time.","There isn't much time.","There aren't much time.","There isn't many time."],"answer":"There isn't much time.","explanation":"Uncountable → much / How much / a little.","explanation_ar":"غير المعدود ← much."},{"q":"My grandpa drinks ___ coffee.","options":["a lot","much of","many","a lot of"],"answer":"a lot of","explanation":"Positive sentences → a lot of (with of).","explanation_ar":"الإثبات ← a lot of."},{"q":"Add ___ lemon juice.","options":["lot","a little","a few","many"],"answer":"a little","explanation":"a few (countable) • a little (uncountable).","explanation_ar":"a few للمعدود وa little لغير المعدود."},{"q":"a ___ of tomatoes","options":["loaf","piece","can","slice"],"answer":"can","explanation":"Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"a ___ of cheese","options":["carton","bottle","jar","slice"],"answer":"slice","explanation":"Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."},{"q":"four ___ of water","options":["bottle","bottles","bottless","bottles'"],"answer":"bottles","explanation":"Make the container plural, not the food.","explanation_ar":"اجمع الوعاء لا الطعام."},{"q":"___ the soup with a big spoon.","options":["Stir","Chop","Fry it","Bake"],"answer":"Stir","explanation":"Choose the cooking verb that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر فعل الطبخ المناسب."},{"q":"___ the potatoes in hot oil.","options":["Pour","Mix it","Fry","Bake"],"answer":"Fry","explanation":"Choose the cooking verb that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر فعل الطبخ المناسب."},{"q":"Something you use to mix food in is a ___.","options":["spoon","jar","carton","bowl"],"answer":"bowl","explanation":"Choose the kitchen word that fits.","explanation_ar":"اختر كلمة المطبخ المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["We need, rice, chicken, and onions.","We need rice, chicken, onions and.","We need rice chicken and onions.","We need rice, chicken, and onions."],"answer":"We need rice, chicken, and onions.","explanation":"Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["Chop the onions fry them and add the meat.","Chop the onions, fry them, and add the meat.","Chop the onions, fry them, add the meat and.","Chop, the onions fry them, and add the meat."],"answer":"Chop the onions, fry them, and add the meat.","explanation":"Phrases and actions in a series also need commas.","explanation_ar":"العبارات والأفعال تحتاج فواصل أيضًا."},{"q":"","options":["I'd like bread, and honey.","I'd like bread and honey.","I'd like, bread and honey.","I'd like bread, honey."],"answer":"I'd like bread and honey.","explanation":"Two items → no comma.","explanation_ar":"عنصران ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"How many commas? \"Do you want tea coffee or juice?\"","options":["0","3","2","1"],"answer":"2","explanation":"Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"","options":["Grandma, Mom, and Sara made the cookies.",", Grandma, Mom and Sara made the cookies.","Grandma, Mom, and, Sara made the cookies.","Grandma Mom and Sara made the cookies."],"answer":"Grandma, Mom, and Sara made the cookies.","explanation":"No comma before the first item.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة قبل العنصر الأول."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a recipe:","options":["Add a few salt, a little olives, and some cheeses.","Add a little salt a few olives and some cheese.","Add a little salt, a few olives, and some cheese.","Add, a little salt, a few olives, and some cheese."],"answer":"Add a little salt, a few olives, and some cheese.","explanation":"Three or more items → commas and and/or before the last.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة عناصر أو أكثر ← فواصل."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"how much eggs do we need\"","options":["how many eggs do we need?","How many egg do we need?","How much eggs do we need?","How many eggs do we need?"],"answer":"How many eggs do we need?","explanation":"Countable → many / How many / a few.","explanation_ar":"المعدود ← many."},{"q":"Is there any milk? – ___","options":["Yes, there's a carton in the fridge.","Yes, there are some milks.","Yes, there's a milk in the fridge.","Yes, there's many milk."],"answer":"Yes, there's a carton in the fridge.","explanation":"Use the right container or quantity word.","explanation_ar":"استخدم الوعاء المناسب."}],"theme_ar":"هيا نطبخ!","essential_question_ar":"كيف يجمع الطبخُ العائلات؟","can_do":"I can talk about food with countable and uncountable nouns, some, any, much, many and a lot of, and write a simple recipe.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الطعام بالأسماء المعدودة وغير المعدودة وsome وany وmuch وmany وa lot of، وأكتب وصفة بسيطة."});
